Mitcad's patch to OCCT 8.0.1, under OCCT's licence:
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

A window-less EGL context: OpenGl_Window::init() selects the colour
buffer of the default FBO it has just made, not GL_BACK (mitcad#2031).

Expected: a view attached to an EGL context that is current without a
surface (EGL_KHR_surfaceless_context, as Qt's offscreen surface on
Wayland is) draws into the offscreen default FBO OpenGl_Window::init()
makes for it, and leaves no GL error behind.
Actual: init() makes and binds that FBO, then calls
SetDrawBuffer(GL_BACK), which binds framebuffer 0 again and calls
glDrawBuffer(GL_BACK). A window-less context has no window framebuffer,
so the driver raises GL_INVALID_OPERATION (NVIDIA 580 on Wayland). The
error stays pending until the next glGetError(): the first frame's
OpenGl_Texture::Init2DMultisample reads it after a successful
glTexStorage2DMultisample and reports "MSAA texture ... cannot be
created with error GL_INVALID_OPERATION" and "Main FBO initialization
has failed", so the frame is drawn without its scene FBO. Every resize
runs init() again, so every resize repeats it.
Reproducer: an EGL display, a desktop OpenGL 4.5 compatibility context
made current with EGL_NO_SURFACE, an OpenGl_GraphicDriver that names
that display and context (no EGL config), a V3d_View with
NbMsaaSamples 4 and a virtual Aspect_NeutralWindow whose native handle
is EGL_NO_SURFACE: after SetWindow, glGetError() gives
GL_INVALID_OPERATION and framebuffer 0 is bound; a KHR_debug callback
places it in glDrawBuffer from OpenGl_Context::SetDrawBuffer from
OpenGl_Window::init. The same calls give no error and the MSAA texture
is made when that error is not pending.

- OpenGl_Window::init() selects GL_COLOR_ATTACHMENT0 when it made the
  offscreen default FBO (the window-less EGL branch), which keeps that
  FBO bound; otherwise GL_BACK as before. GLX, WGL, EGL with a surface
  and OpenGL ES (where SetDrawBuffer does nothing) are unchanged.

The patch's test and its before/after proof:
third_party/vcpkg-ports/docs/opencascade-patch-tests.md, section 2031.

Upstream: new; changes only the window-less EGL branch, whose comment
says it is never called upstream (a pbuffer is made there when OCCT has
an EGL config).

diff --git a/src/Visualization/TKOpenGl/OpenGl/OpenGl_Window.cxx b/src/Visualization/TKOpenGl/OpenGl/OpenGl_Window.cxx
index 4c7caf381..2a11da18d 100644
--- a/src/Visualization/TKOpenGl/OpenGl/OpenGl_Window.cxx
+++ b/src/Visualization/TKOpenGl/OpenGl/OpenGl_Window.cxx
@@ -860,6 +860,8 @@ void OpenGl_Window::init()
     return;
   }
 
+  // a window-less context has no back buffer: it draws into the default FBO's colour buffer
+  bool toDrawIntoDefaultFbo = false;
   #if defined(HAVE_EGL)
   if ((EGLSurface)myGlContext->myWindow == EGL_NO_SURFACE)
   {
@@ -886,6 +888,7 @@ void OpenGl_Window::init()
     }
     myGlContext->SetDefaultFrameBuffer(aDefFbo);
     aDefFbo->BindBuffer(myGlContext);
+    toDrawIntoDefaultFbo = true;
   }
   else if (!myPlatformWindow->IsVirtual() && mySizeWindow == myPlatformWindow)
   {
@@ -906,7 +909,9 @@ void OpenGl_Window::init()
   myGlContext->core11fwd->glDisable(GL_SCISSOR_TEST);
   const int aViewport[4] = {0, 0, mySize.x(), mySize.y()};
   myGlContext->ResizeViewport(aViewport);
-  myGlContext->SetDrawBuffer(GL_BACK);
+  // GL_BACK would bind the window's framebuffer again, which a window-less context does not
+  // have (GL_INVALID_OPERATION, left for the next glGetError() to find)
+  myGlContext->SetDrawBuffer(toDrawIntoDefaultFbo ? GL_COLOR_ATTACHMENT0 : GL_BACK);
   if (myGlContext->core11ffp != nullptr)
   {
     myGlContext->core11ffp->glMatrixMode(GL_MODELVIEW);
